  "tldr": [
    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Gemini refused to give me the lyrics to Twinkle Twinkle Little Star",
      "url": "https://www.comentr.com/technology/01M88DWQ0R4NCMYR17AFEWRG1F",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50638320",
      "score": 212,
      "comments": 163,
      "author": "hoodied",
      "published": "2026-11-25T04:03:33Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Google Gemini's automated copyright guardrails mistakenly flag public domain text, blocking benign queries due to overly aggressive IP filtering.",
        "Aggressive post-processing and safety alignment introduce high false-positive refusal rates, degrading model utility on standard, non-infringing retrieval tasks.",
        "Production LLM systems require public-domain allowlists and context-aware heuristics rather than blanket, naive copyright matching mechanisms."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Fund browser-grade certificate checking for every TLS client",
      "url": "https://upki.rustls.dev/funding.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/mcrzxl",
      "score": 13,
      "comments": 2,
      "author": "wofo",
      "published": "2026-11-24T18:27:49Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Non-browser TLS clients routinely lack robust revocation checking, CRLite, and Certificate Transparency verification, lagging significantly behind modern web browsers.",
        "Standardizing browser-grade X.509 validation across runtimes requires dedicated funding for open-source TLS stacks like OpenSSL, Rustls, and language standard libraries.",
        "Closing this verification gap prevents silent MITM attacks and misissued CA certificate exploitation across backend services, SDKs, and CLI utilities."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Slow Ubuntu security response times",
      "url": "https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/11/25/9",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/wzlzlh",
      "score": 8,
      "comments": 0,
      "author": "hanno",
      "published": "2026-11-25T20:10:24Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Delayed Canonical USN releases prolong enterprise exposure windows to known CVEs compared to faster upstream Debian or RHEL patch cycles.",
        "Security updates lag heavily in Ubuntu's 'universe' repository, frequently leaving unpatched vulnerabilities unless subscribed to Ubuntu Pro ESM.",
        "SecOps teams must actively monitor distribution patch latency and implement compensating controls like container scanning or minimal distroless images."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "devops",
      "title": "Cloudflare hides shortcomings of the underlying infrastructure",
      "url": "https://charlie.fish/posts/2026/11/what-cloudflare-doesnt-tell-you/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50632883",
      "score": 164,
      "comments": 105,
      "author": "fishcharlie",
      "published": "2026-11-24T19:03:55Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Aggressive edge caching and DDoS mitigation mask underlying database bottlenecks, leaving fragile origin services exposed during sudden cache misses.",
        "Relying on Cloudflare for performance creates false reliability, risking cascading infrastructure failures if traffic patterns bypass the CDN layer.",
        "Edge proxies obscure true origin telemetry, complicating root-cause analysis and masking internal connection exhaustion or compute capacity issues."
      ]
    },
    {
